--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Architecture (matches established sibling W7 page AlertRulesPage in the same domain)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- MVVM, no business logic in code-behind. The view binds AlertsListPageViewModel and
  renders the pure AlertsListDisplay projection; all branch selection / formatting /
  i18n / aggregate maths happen in the headless Model. State changes are marshalled
  onto the UI thread via DispatcherQueue.
- Data port IAlertsFeed (web hooks) -> generated C# OpenAPI client (ADR-004):
    useAlerts          -> get_api_v1_alerts                     GET  /alerts
    useAlertRules      -> get_api_v1_alerts_rules               GET  /alerts/rules
    usePinned          -> get_api_v1_pinned (?type=alert_rule)  GET  /pinned
    useMarkAlertRead   -> post_api_v1_alerts_alertID_read       POST /alerts/{id}/read
    useAcknowledgeAlert-> post_api_v1_alerts_alertID_acknowledge POST /alerts/{id}/acknowledge { note }
    useReopenAlert     -> post_api_v1_alerts_alertID_reopen     POST /alerts/{id}/reopen
    useAlertDetail     -> get_api_v1_alerts_alertID             GET  /alerts/{id}
  (op ids cross-checked against apps/windows/Generated ApiEndpoints.All — all present.)
- Shared Fluent components reused (no web pixel-cloning, ADR-005/006):
    PageTitle/Subhead (header), TsBadge (quiet-hours + pinned status), TsSkeleton (loading,
    5 rows), TsErrorDisplay (error), TsEmptyState (empty + overview-empty + list-empty),
    TsGlassPanel (overview / trend / type / pinned regions), TsMetricCard x6 (KPI tiles),
    TsBarChart (7-day severity trend), TsPieChart (by-type donut + legend), TsInlineCallout
    (critical callout + acknowledge toast w/ undo), TsSearchInput (search), TsButton
    (filter tabs / pagination / chip-remove / active-rules link), AlertCard (the already-
    ported shared card surface — reused for every list row), TsTextarea + ContentDialog
    (acknowledge note + audit-timeline modal).
- The per-alert "View context" drill-through is a 1:1 port of web/src/lib/alertDrillthrough.ts
  (SIGNAL_TO_PAGE map + snake_case vehicle_id/t/signal query) in AlertsListRegistration.DrillthroughHref.
- i18n: every visible literal flows through ILocalizer.GetString("<key>","<English fallback>").
  Per the established W7 contract the page keys resolve through the WinUI resource bridge and
  fall back to the verbatim web English copy; headless tests assert every key is requested
  (RecordingLocalizer). Key names match the web manifest verbatim.
- Units: this page has no SI-unit fields (alert counts / read-rate %); nothing stored/computed non-SI.
- Live data: the web page is a TanStack query only (no live/SSE source), so no >2min staleness
  chrome is applicable (matches the web source).

